(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[26 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [29 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [30 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [31 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [32 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [33 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [34 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [35 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [36 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [37 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [38 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [39 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [62 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [109 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [130 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [134 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [162 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [170 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [185 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [186 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [203 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [242 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [243 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [244 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [256 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [301 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [302 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [328 62 "// a fallback root's constraint"] [364 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [388 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [407 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [408 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [409 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [410 1 "// labels after it."] [446 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [448 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [462 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [477 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_error_string's form of a reason: lower case, words apart."] [495 1 "// raiseErr is PySSL_SetError for an operation's Go error: the exception CPython's _ssl raises for what OpenSSL"] [496 1 "// would have reported."] [539 1 "// ---- the transport's two ends on the Python side ----"] [556 1 "// need is how much the record being fed still needs: its header's rest, then its body's."] [572 16 "// not a TLS record: the engine refuses its header"] [586 1 "// fill feeds the engine the next bytes of the current record: false when they are not there yet (a"] [587 1 "// non-blocking socket, an empty incoming BIO)."] [645 1 "// flush sends what the engine wrote: into the outgoing BIO, or to the socket (a non-blocking one's rest kept,"] [646 1 "// SSLWantWriteError)."] [703 1 "// step hands control to the engine, starting op (nil: resuming it), until it waits for input or is done; the"] [704 1 "// callbacks it asks for run here."] [725 1 "// drive runs an engine operation (resuming the one in flight first) to its end: OpenSSL's loop of SSL_do_handshake"] [726 1 "// or SSL_read with the socket's waits; SSLWantReadError when its input is not there yet."] [791 1 "// ---- the methods ----"] [805 2 "// close_notify received: SSL_read's zero return is 0 bytes while it is the only shutdown seen"] [806 2 "// (SSL_RECEIVED_SHUTDOWN), SSLZeroReturnError once this side sent its own"] [907 27 "// the peer closed the transport: SSL_shutdown's second call gives up"] [922 1 "// ---- wrap ----"] [1037 1 "// ---- SSLSession ----"] [1048 1 "// ---- MemoryBIO ----"] [1215 21 "// SSL_get_client_ciphers is a server's"] [1302 4 "// a resumed session keeps its id and time (a ticket the server renewed only replaces its state)"] [1313 30 "// OpenSSL's session of a connection that got no ticket (yet)"] [1324 2 "// SSLSession"] [1346 2 "// MemoryBIO"] [1396 1 "// ---- PKCS #8 encryption (PBES2 with PBKDF2, RFC 8018), which Go's x509 does not read ----"] [1494 1 "// sslTimeout is the TimeoutError of an operation past the socket's timeout (the handshake's message with"] [1495 1 "// ERRSTR's prefix, as _ssl.c has it)."] [1503 1 "// sslPBKDF2 is RFC 8018's PBKDF2 with HMAC over prf (crypto/pbkdf2's Key is generic, which goi's table does not"] [1504 1 "// call)."] [1530 1 "// sslDistrustedSPKI are the SHA-256 digests of the public keys _ssl refuses in any chain (Modules/_ssl/"] [1531 1 "// distrusted_spki.h, gh-160040: the compromised eMudhra intermediates)."] [1554 1 "// afterHandshake is what OpenSSL keeps of a finished handshake: the context's session statistics, and the"] [1555 1 "// anchor its by-hash lookup loaded from a capath directory, now in the store (get_ca_certs lists it)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[86 25] [189 39] [190 26] [197 24] [230 38] [266 25] [395 38] [396 63] [412 28] [519 29] [550 19] [730 42] [783 43] [846 57] [854 28] [858 19] [861 32] [864 56] [874 27] [881 19] [889 34] [913 59] [966 44] [982 31] [1012 31] [1081 28] [1087 33] [1148 33] [1364 33] [1509 16] [1509 35] [1515 13] [1515 23] [1519 14] [1519 21] [1528 54] [1570 25]] :go/trails [[459 127] [474 76] [1540 68]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl_conn.go" :imports [


